# PLAN-977 B-PY-V — the py-977 tracked corpus: the legacy a2p public
# obligations through the `ac-a2py/hir-stdlib-run-v1` CASE line (the
# `ac_a2py_hir` adapter -> prebuilt a2x-worker `run-py` -> REAL OS
# Python 3.14, parent-side judged; the worker never sees expectations).
#
# Observation axes (V: 返回/输出/短路/异常/资源): value returns
# (value/generic), stdout observation face, short-circuit trace marks on
# stderr, trap faces (overflow/div-zero), and the record-text explicit
# lifecycle lane (value-level here; the zero-leak trace proof lives in
# the 1042 pyready suite and the p977 crate-level probe). Routing facts
# frozen by B-PY-I; the List/packages leg rides the crate-level suite
# (the case line is single-file). Independent hand oracles throughout.

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace.m2.p977.py.value"
  tags: ["ace-m2", "py-977", "plan-977"]
  links: ["PLAN-977"]
  source: { file: "src/value.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "py-run", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: { recipe: "ac-a2py/hir-stdlib-run-v1", a2x_hir: { profile: "scalar", entry: "main", caps: [] }, steps: [{ op: "run" }] },
      expect: { completion: "success", stdout: { text: "value:14\n", compare: "bytes" } } }
  ]
}
```

